xnu 0479: start the wifi worker after the whole probe block

Measured 2026-11-26 across five boots: any `ml_io_map()` taken while another
boot probe is mapping wedges that thread. The wifi pin premap stops the block at
the eUSB2 map when it runs at the top (0475, 0476, 0478) and stops itself when
it runs inside `usb_probe()` (0477), while `0474` -- no boot-time pin premap --
prints `probe done`. The worker itself stops at `early GCC` when it starts
inside `usb_probe()` and maps the pins while the block is still mapping (0474).

The pin premap leaves the boot block, and the worker starts as the last
statement of the block, after the BT registration. Its first act is then
`wifi_map_pins()` with no other mapper running, and it still finds the BAR,
config, DBI, ELBI, iATU, PARF/PHY, AHB and SMMU windows premapped.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index fe2fb0f..5379e5e 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -2402,6 +2402,7 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		extern void mondrian_spmi_probe(void);
 		extern void mondrian_reset_reason_init(void);
 		extern void mondrian_wifi_premap(void);
+		extern void mondrian_wifi_start(void);
 
 		/*
 		 * The premap takes every window the wifi worker touches before
@@ -2420,6 +2421,14 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		mondrian_venus_start();
 		mondrian_bt_tty_init();
 		mondrian_bt_ctl_init();
+		/*
+		 * Last, with the whole probe block done: the worker maps the
+		 * TLMM pin pages itself, and mapping them at the top of the
+		 * block or beside a probe that is still mapping wedges the
+		 * mapper (measured 2026-11-26, five boots stopped at a
+		 * different point each time).
+		 */
+		mondrian_wifi_start();
 	}
 }
 
